  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nUpper ridging over the western and central portions of the U.S.\nextends into eastern Montana through the beginning of the week,\ncontinuing the warm, but seasonally average, temperatures. Given\nNE Montana will be on the northeast quadrant of the ridge under\nnorthwest flow aloft, a weak embedded shortwave may be enough to\nset off a few isolated showers around mid-day today. \n\nFor Wednesday into Friday, upper ridging amplifies as the ridge \naxis pushes across central Montana and adjacent Canada with a \nwarming trend resuming. Conditions will largely be dry save for an\nisolated thunderstorm forming over the central Montana mountains \nin the afternoon with the diurnal heating and instability, and the\nweak embedded disturbances that might drag it across northeast \nMontana in the evening hours. Most places however will remain dry \nthrough this period. As of now monsoonal moisture looks to remain \njust south of the region across southern Montana, giving an \noverall drier setup.\n\nThe ridge axis will begin to slide east Into the region on Friday\ninto the weekend, lending to a return to triple digit heat across \nthe area as well as a continuation of thunderstorm chances at \ntimes. If the current ensemble means hold, eventual heat related \nproducts will be necessary. Some ensemble members begin to slide \nthe ridge axis farther east into North Dakota Sunday night through\nTuesday which should open up higher chance for monsoonal showers \nacross the region and may drop temps a little into early next \nweek. But confidence in this ridge axis slide is low. \n\nHaze from smoke across Washington and Oregon has thankfully not \nquite reduced visibility below 10 SM, and therefore has not yet \nbecome nuisance enough to place in the grids directly. So, Big \nSky Country may have to wait awhile longer to get its namesake \nback. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nChanged hourly default NBM PPI01 PoPs with a CAMs Blend of NPoPs\nfor mentionable mid-day shower chances today. Ensemble consensus \nis fairly solid depicting upper ridging over the foreseeable \nfuture. No changes to NBM otherwise.\n\nGAH",
